  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "My SDK version: VRChat SDK AVATAR 2021.11.24.16.20\nVRChat docs say that VRChat/Mobile/Particles shaders are made for avatar particles and worlds.\nhttps://docs.vrchat.com/docs/quest-content-limitations#components\nHowever, they won't work with Particle Systems on avatars.\nTo be precise, they draw nothing for particles.\nI tested various patterns for Render module: Billboard x [ToonLit, Additive, Multiply], Mesh x [...].\nYou can see particles with ToonLit shader, but Additive and Multiply doesn't draw anything (even the pink box).\nThe questions:\nIs this an intended behavior; VRChat teams just forgot to update docs that you can no longer use particle shaders with Particle Systems on quest avatars?\nOR\nDid I forget something for particle shaders to work with avatar particles?\nOR\nIs this just a bug?\nSincerely yours.",
